<h1>Best <em>Plyo Boxes</em> for Vertical Jump Training</h1>
<div class="hero-meta">
<span class="hero-meta-item">📖 7 min read</span>
<span class="hero-meta-item">📦 Gear Guide</span>
<span class="hero-meta-item">📈 Vertical Jump</span>
</div>
<p class="hero-intro">
    A plyo box is the one piece of equipment every jump program uses. The right one depends on how high you jump now and how you'll use it. Here's how to pick the right height and material, plus five boxes worth buying.
  </p>
</div><div class="article-wrap">
<div class="content">
<div class="callout">
<div class="callout-icon">⚡</div>
<div class="callout-text"><strong>Quick answer:</strong> Most athletes should buy a <strong>soft 3-in-1 foam box</strong> sized to their vertical. Under a 26-inch vertical, get 16/20/24 inches; above that, 20/24/30. Heavier athletes should choose a wood-core padded box with a higher weight rating.</div>
</div>
<h2 id="what-height">What Height Box Do You Need?</h2>
<p>The most common box jump mistake is buying, or jumping onto, a box that's too high. A box jump only builds power if you land in roughly the same knee bend you took off in. When the box is too high, you end up pulling your knees to your chest and landing in a deep squat. That trains hip mobility, not jumping.</p>
<p>Use your current vertical to choose your working height. If you don't know it, measure it and run it through the <a href="/vertical-jump-percentile">vertical jump calculator</a> first.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="data-table">
<thead><tr><th>Your Vertical</th><th>Working Box Height</th><th>Box to Buy</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Under 20"</td><td>12–16"</td><td>Stackable or small 3-in-1</td></tr>
<tr class="highlight"><td>20–26"</td><td>16–20"</td><td>3-in-1 (16/20/24)</td></tr>
<tr class="highlight"><td>26–32"</td><td>20–24"</td><td>3-in-1 (16/20/24 or 20/24/30)</td></tr>
<tr><td>32"+</td><td>24–30"</td><td>3-in-1 (20/24/30)</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong>Depth jumps are different.</strong> For a depth jump you step <em>off</em> the box, land and rebound instantly, so the box height is a drop height. Keep it low: 12 inches for beginners and no more than about 18 inches for trained athletes. Higher drops slow your ground contact and turn a reactive-power drill into a landing drill.</p>
<h2 id="soft-vs-wood">Soft vs. Wood vs. Steel</h2>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="data-table">
<thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Best For</th><th>Trade-off</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr class="highlight"><td>Soft foam</td><td>Box jumps near your max, younger athletes, home gyms</td><td>Slightly softer takeoff; capacity varies</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wood core + foam</td><td>Heavier athletes, jumps plus step-ups</td><td>Heavier and pricier</td></tr>
<tr><td>Plywood</td><td>Step-ups, split squats, low-height jumps</td><td>Hard edges punish missed jumps</td></tr>
<tr><td>Steel adjustable</td><td>Gyms that need many heights</td><td>Expensive; least forgiving surface</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>For vertical jump training specifically, soft wins. Jump quality depends on committing fully to each rep, and athletes hesitate on hard boxes. Remove the fear of a shin scrape and most athletes jump noticeably higher.</p>
<h2 id="what-to-look-for">What to Look For</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Footprint:</strong> A wider base means a more stable landing. Avoid tall boxes with small tops.</li>
<li><strong>Weight capacity:</strong> Aim well above your bodyweight, especially if you'll add a weighted vest or do loaded step-ups.</li>
<li><strong>Surface grip:</strong> Textured vinyl or anti-slip tops matter on landings and when the box is used on a smooth floor.</li>
<li><strong>Three heights in one:</strong> A 3-in-1 box changes height when you flip it, so it grows with you as your vertical improves.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="the-picks">The 5 Best Plyo Boxes</h2>
<p>These picks are based on build, height options and weight ratings from the manufacturers' listings, matched to how athletes actually train. Prices change often, so check the current price before you buy.</p>
<div class="pick">
<div class="pick-badge">Best soft box for most athletes</div>
<h3>BalanceFrom 3-in-1 Foam Plyo Box</h3>
<ul class="pick-specs"><li>Foam</li><li>3 heights in one</li><li>Sold in 16/20/24 and 20/24/30</li><li>Lightweight</li></ul>
<p><strong>Why it's here:</strong> The simplest way to get a forgiving box with three training heights. The foam surface means a missed jump costs you a bruise, not a gashed shin, which is exactly what you want when you're pushing toward your max height.</p><p><strong>Who it's for:</strong> Most high school and adult athletes training box jumps at home. Pick the 16/20/24 size if your vertical is under about 26 inches; the 20/24/30 size if you're already jumping higher.</p><p><strong>Watch out for:</strong> Weight capacity varies by size, and the compact version is rated lower than most boxes here (around 220 lb). Heavier athletes or anyone using a weighted vest should check the listing or choose the next pick.</p>
<a class="pick-btn" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=BalanceFrom%203-in-1%20foam%20plyometric%20jump%20box&amp;tag=athletecalc-20" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Check price on Amazon ↗</a>
</div><div class="pick">
<div class="pick-badge">Best for heavier athletes</div>
<h3>Yes4All 3-in-1 Soft-Padded Plyo Box</h3>
<ul class="pick-specs"><li>Wood core, foam shell</li><li>3 heights in one</li><li>Listed up to 450 lb</li></ul>
<p><strong>Why it's here:</strong> A wood frame inside a padded cover gives you a firmer, more stable takeoff than all-foam boxes while still protecting your shins. That higher capacity makes it the safer choice for linemen, bigger athletes and weighted step-ups.</p><p><strong>Who it's for:</strong> Athletes over about 200 lb, or anyone who wants one box for box jumps, step-ups and rear-foot-elevated split squats.</p><p><strong>Watch out for:</strong> It's heavier than foam-only boxes, so it's less convenient to move around a garage or carry to a field.</p>
<a class="pick-btn" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Yes4All%203-in-1%20soft%20padded%20wooden%20plyo%20box&amp;tag=athletecalc-20" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Check price on Amazon ↗</a>
</div><div class="pick">
<div class="pick-badge">Best for depth jumps & progression</div>
